This patch fixes the BGE (Branch if Greater-or-Equal) instruction bug.
Apply to IMDb repository models: Rocket and Piccolo.
NOTE: Pico already has the correct implementation and does not need this patch.

Root cause: ILAng compiler incorrectly translates >= operator for signed comparisons.
The >= operator gets compiled to unsigned greater-than (bvugt) instead of signed
greater-or-equal (bvsge), missing the equality case entirely.

Fix: Use explicit Sge() function (signed greater-or-equal) instead of >= operator,
matching the pattern already used in Pico core.

Impact: BGE instruction will correctly branch when rs1 == rs2 (equality case).

================================================================================
PATCH 1/2: Rocket
================================================================================
File: IMDb/IMDb_Cores/ILA_Rocket/src/riscvIla.cc
Line: 175-184

--- a/IMDb/IMDb_Cores/ILA_Rocket/src/riscvIla.cc
+++ b/IMDb/IMDb_Cores/ILA_Rocket/src/riscvIla.cc
@@ -179,7 +179,8 @@
       auto decode = (opcode == BRANCH) & (funct3 == BGE);
       instr.SetDecode(decode);

-      instr.SetUpdate(pc, Ite(rs1_val >= rs2_val, BTarget, NC));
+      // Fixed: Use Sge() for signed greater-or-equal (>= operator is buggy in ILAng)
+      instr.SetUpdate(pc, Ite(Sge(rs1_val, rs2_val), BTarget, NC));
       RECORD_INST("BGE");
     }

